hyprland-preview-share-picker (0.2.1-0oaxaca1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Initial Oaxaca package of hyprland-preview-share-picker 0.2.1
    (roadmap step 6). Omarchy v4.0.4 installs the program and names
    the binary as custom_picker_binary in config/hypr/xdph.conf, so
    xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland opens the picker, with window and monitor
    previews, on every screen-share request. Ubuntu's archive has no
    hyprland-preview-share-picker.
  * The upstream tarball is the GitHub release tag; the hyprland-protocols
    git submodule, which the tarball ships as an empty directory, comes as
    the component "hyprland-protocols" at the commit Omarchy's recipe pins
    (3a5c2bda1c1a4e55cc1330c782547695a93f05b2); the crates from Cargo.lock
    come as the component "vendor", made by cargo vendor on the build host.
    See the "upstream" file next to debian/.
  * d/patches/build-rs-no-git.patch: build.rs sets GIT_VERSION to a fixed
    string instead of running git, as Omarchy's recipe does.
  * d/rules: links lib/hyprland-protocols to the component, points cargo at
    the vendored crates, builds with cargo build --frozen --release, and
    installs the binary and the schema.json the binary prints.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
